==============================================================================
THE 27B's EMBEDDING ROW — the one number that decides ONE board vs TWO
==============================================================================
  27B W4 g128 weight pack             12.485 GiB
  embedding, NATURAL row 10240 B      2.368 GiB -> total  14.853 GiB of 16.000  (92.8 %)  FITS
  embedding, PADDED  row 16384 B     3.789 GiB -> total  16.274 GiB of 16.000  (101.7 %)  OVER
  the padding costs 1455 MiB and the overflow is 281 MiB — so the 27B's one-board verdict turns entirely on EMBLOG2.
  NOTE the padded row needs EMBLOG2 = 14, one MORE than the 13 the
  shipped 9B uses (NEXT_SESSION.md 1).

==============================================================================
THE LOADER — GiB to push into a host-less board B, and how long
==============================================================================
Board B has POWER ONLY: no PCIe, no XDMA, no BAR.  Everything below
crosses the QSFP28 link once per model load (E: rates assumed, see
the RATES table; no link has been built or measured).

assumed payload rates (GB/s, 1 GB = 1e9 B):
   Aurora 64B/66B x4 (ideal payload)              12.500
   Aurora 64B/66B x4 @ 90 % of that               11.250
   100GbE CMAC x4, 9000 B jumbo UDP               12.406
   100GbE CMAC x4, 1500 B MTU UDP                 11.945
   Aurora 64B/66B x1 lane                          3.125
   10GbE SFP+ (snoke's 82599), 1500 B UDP          1.158

